# Placeholder — overwritten by Ansible's "Backend-CA-Bundle (Caddy Root +
# certifi) erzeugen" task on every deploy, right after Caddy's first start
# (Caddy's self-signed root CA only exists after that). Committed so the
# docker-compose.staging.yml/prod.yml bind mount always has a real file to
# mount on a brand new host, instead of Docker creating an empty directory
# in its place when the source path doesn't exist yet.
#
# See claude_docs/HANDOVER.md for why this exists at all: Moodle currently
# runs with `tls internal` (Caddy self-signs) because certificates.dhbw.cloud
# (HARICA) has a server-side bug blocking the real ACME certificate. Once
# that's resolved and Moodle gets a real cert, this whole mechanism —
# this file, the Ansible task that builds it, and the REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE
# env var pointing at it — should be removed.
